### [rule] Claude Code LLM spans must be emitted per logical assistant message, not per JSONL entry  (id: claude-code-llm-spans-must-be-emitted-per-logical-assistant, confidence 80%)
Symptom: In MLflow traces of Claude Code sessions, assistant turns that only call tools or only contain thinking show no token usage or cost, and a message split across several transcript lines is undercounted.
Root cause: libs/typescript/integrations/claude-code/src/tracing.ts:createLlmAndToolSpans created the LLM span only when the entry had non-empty text and no tool_use, so tool-only and thinking-only entries produced no usage or cost.
Fix pattern: Build one logical message per message.id with getLogicalAssistantMessage (concatenate content, field-merge usage, keep the first known model), create one LLM span per message key via emittedLlmMessageKeys, and still emit one tool span per tool_use block from the original entry.
Constraints: Coalesce only by message.id; entries without an id stay independent (keyed by transcript index). Do not sum usage fields, because Claude Code repeats the full per-message usage on split entries and summing double counts. Skip progress rows while coalescing but break on any other non-assistant entry such as user, so separate turns that reuse an id are not merged.
Applies: Claude Code transcript parsing in libs/typescript/integrations/claude-code; the Python tracer in mlflow/claude_code is not changed by this change.
→ pointers: libs/typescript/integrations/claude-code/src/tracing.ts:getLogicalAssistantMessage:L186 [1 call site in 1 file], libs/typescript/integrations/claude-code/src/tracing.ts:createLlmAndToolSpans:L372 [4 call sites in 2 files]

### [rule] CI auto-retry eligibility is opt-in via the auto-rerun label, not author or auto-merge  (id: ci-auto-retry-eligibility-is-opt-in-via-the-auto-rerun-label, confidence 80%)
Symptom: a PR that failed CI is never retried automatically, even though it is open, non-draft and recent.
Root cause: .github/workflows/retry.yml, the gh api graphql search in the candidate step, selects PRs by the search string `label:auto-rerun` (plus `is:open draft:false created:>=$cutoff`), not by `author:app/dependabot` or an autoMergeRequest.
Fix pattern: to make a PR eligible, add the `auto-rerun` label. Do not reintroduce author or auto-merge filters in the search or the jq `select`.
Constraints: Only the mergeable != CONFLICTING jq filter, the three-day cutoff, pagination, retry limits and dry-run still apply. The label must exist in the repository before anything applies it.
Applies: Eligibility for the automatic CI retry sweep in this repository.
Applies: Candidate selection for the automatic CI retry sweep only; not the retry.sh rerun logic itself.
